// DomainRecon V2 bundled public-suffix SUBSET (offline, Public Suffix List rule syntax).
//
// This file is a curated, conservative subset of https://publicsuffix.org/list/ (MPL-2.0).
// It is NOT the complete list. DomainRecon combines it with a fail-closed heuristic
// (generic second-level label + two-letter country-code TLD) so that common registry
// suffixes such as co.uk or com.sa are rejected as root targets without any network access.
//
// To use the authoritative list instead, place an unmodified copy of the official
// public_suffix_list.dat at domainrecon\data\public_suffix_list.dat, or point the
// DOMAINRECON_PSL_FILE environment variable at it. When the full list is present the
// heuristic is disabled and only the official rules apply. DomainRecon never downloads it.
//
// Syntax: one rule per line; "*." wildcard rules and "!" exception rules are supported.
// IDN rules are stored in their ASCII (punycode) form.

